Loom: address realization for loops without an exact header-tested recurrence (runtime bound, bottom-tested exit).
Such loops get a realization domain with no induction and an estimated trip count for costs only (the alternating
LDS bank still needs an exact induction) and may offer from any uniform body block; exact loops keep the latch rule.
Global loads whose loop-varying terms are all uniform move them out of the vector address: the descriptor carries the
uniform invariant terms plus the largest-stride varying term, the rest go to the packet's scalar offset, and the
lane terms become one hoisted vector component. R2P attention: paged K/V staging loads become buffer loads with
SALU-built descriptors; 8K 753.9 -> 742.6 Mcyc, 16K 2910.8 -> 2872.4; bit-identical results.
